//// rakun-app — the server half of the Next.js `app/` router.
////
//// Front 22's file-convention route registry and `app/` scan (`file_router`)
//// and front 23's SSR pipeline and page dispatch (`ssr`), relocated out of the
//// core by front 95 (`specs/1.0.10-beta/03-rakun/modules.md` § The cut): a
//// Spring-style REST service never loads them, and nothing in the core imports
//// either. Fronts 24, 25, 60, 61, 63, 64 and 66 land here too. Reached by a
//// consumer via `import {…} from "rakun-app"`; the core's surface (`Request`,
//// `Response`, `rkProp`, the request context) is imported `from "rakun"`.
////
//// The host halves ship beside the code: `sidecars/rakun_file_router.erl` /
//// `sidecars/rakun_ssr.erl` (erlang-only, decision 113).

// `file_router` before `ssr`: front 23's pipeline imports it, and the `files`
// ORDER in `botopink.json` is a dependency order a consumer's build reads
// literally.
pub mod file_router;
pub mod ssr;
